sequenceDiagram
    actor User as Operator
    participant RL as JobsListSubcommand
    participant RT as JobsTerminateSubcommand
    participant EC2 as AWS EC2
    participant DDB as DynamoDB<br/><prefix>-results

    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
        Note over User,DDB: baas jobs list [--limit 20] [--in-flight] [--project p] [--tag k=v]... [--format table|json|csv]
        User->>RL: baas jobs list --in-flight
        RL->>EC2: describeInstances(tag baas-role=benchmark-runner, baas-deployment=prefix, state=pending|running)
        EC2-->>RL: live instances, each with its baas-job-id tag
        Note over RL: ONE call, bounded by what is running -- not by how many jobs vanished
        loop pages of 100, newest first, until --limit rows match
            RL->>DDB: Query pk = JOB, ScanIndexForward=false
            DDB-->>RL: job items
        end
        Note over RL: stored terminal status -> shown as is.<br/>Non-terminal + live instance with its job id -> in flight.<br/>Non-terminal + no live instance -> vanished (computed, never written),<br/>but only once the job is 5 min old: a younger one keeps its stored status (R12).<br/>Nothing is hidden: exclude_from_results runs are listed, with their source.
        RL-->>User: JOB_ID | PROJECT | STATUS | SOURCE | INSTANCE | INSTANCE_TYPE | STARTED | ELAPSED<br/>or "No jobs in flight." -- exit 0
    end

    rect rgb(255, 245, 235)
        Note over User,DDB: baas jobs terminate <jobId> [--yes]
        User->>RT: baas jobs terminate 20261003T070025527Z-5bc8461b
        RT->>DDB: Query jobId-index (gsi1pk = jobId, gsi1sk = JOB), then GetItem by its key, strongly consistent
        alt no job item in this deployment
            RT-->>User: "No job found", exit 1 -- nothing is terminated (R6)
        end
        RT->>EC2: describeInstances(instanceId), else by the job-id tag AND baas-deployment
        alt terminal status and no live instance
            RT-->>User: "already ended", exit 0 -- nothing changed
        else completed, failed:n or timed-out with a live instance
            RT-->>User: "already ended, terminates itself", exit 0 -- left to upload its boot log (R10)
        end
        Note over RT: confirm: a terminal prompts [y/N], --yes skips,<br/>no terminal and no --yes refuses
        Note over RT,EC2: JobStop -- the same step as JobSession.stop (R8)
        RT->>DDB: UpdateItem status cancelled (5 s timeout, never over a terminal status)
        alt refused, and a strong re-read shows completed, failed:n or timed-out
            RT-->>User: "already ended, terminates itself", exit 0 -- the instance won the race
        else written, refused over cancelled, or the write failed
            RT->>EC2: terminateInstances(liveInstance)
            alt termination fails
                RT-->>User: error naming the instance, exit 1
            else
                RT-->>User: terminated, exit 0
            end
        end
    end
